# Trivy CVE Exceptions — Chatterly API
# CVEs present in node:20-alpine3.21 base image OS/npm packages
# No upstream fix available in Alpine package repo as of 2026-07-19
#
# Mitigating controls:
#   - TLS termination handled at nginx Ingress layer (not app layer)
#   - App runs in private AKS subnet, not directly internet-exposed
#   - NSG restricts inbound traffic to port 80/443 only
#   - Base image rebuilt weekly via ADO pipeline (auto-picks patches when released)
#   - Prisma-only node_modules in runtime image (minimal attack surface)
#
# Risk accepted by: Osman Khan (Senior DevOps Engineer)
# Review date: 2026-10-01
# Re-run: trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --ignore-unfixed chatterly-api:latest

